  <header class="hero" id="top">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Southern California • Premium Live Music</div>
        <h1>COUNTERTONE</h1>
        <h2>FAMILIAR SONGS. TRANSFORMED LIVE.</h2>
        <p class="hero-copy">A distinctive live music experience where acoustic guitar, vocals and improvisational trumpet weave together in real time—turning familiar songs into something guests don't expect.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a href="#contact" class="btn primary">Check My Date</a>
          <a href="#sound" class="btn">Hear the Difference ↓</a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-note"><span>Corporate Events</span><span>Private Parties</span><span>Weddings</span><span>Curated Atmosphere</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-art" aria-label="Abstract Countertone visual showing two musical lines weaving together">
        <div class="art-box">
          <div class="line1"></div><div class="line2"></div><div class="line3"></div>
          <div class="art-label"><div><div class="small">Acoustic guitar • vocals • trumpet</div><div class="big">The sound lives<br/>between the lines.</div></div><div class="small">COUNTERTONE</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section light" id="sound">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">The difference</div>
        <h2>Not the same old sound for your event.</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">Countertone is built around an unusual musical interaction: John's acoustic guitar and vocals provide the familiar thread, while Shawn's Harmon-muted trumpet answers, echoes and weaves around the melody as another voice.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <div class="quote">“The trumpet isn't just accompanying the song. It becomes part of the conversation.”</div>
          <p class="bio" style="margin-top:28px">The result is a sound that feels <strong>familiar enough to connect immediately</strong> and <strong>different enough to be remembered</strong>. Guests recognize the song—but experience it in a way they likely haven't heard at another event.</p>
          <p class="bio">John Dean makes popular music his own on acoustic guitar and vocals. Shawn Bennion adds soulful, improvisational trumpet and flugelhorn—often using a Harmon mute for the signature smoky tone.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="video-shell">
          <div class="play">▶</div>
          <small>Place Countertone performance video here</small>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="experience">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Your room. Your people. Your moment.</div>
        <h2>We shape the energy you want.</h2>
        <p class="section-lead dark-copy">Some events need elegant music that lets people talk. Others need groove, movement and a moment when the entire room comes alive. Countertone reads the room and adapts the performance to the atmosphere you want to create.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="energy">
        <div><div class="number">01</div><h3>Intimate</h3><p>Warm, close and understated for cocktails, dinners and conversation.</p></div>
        <div><div class="number">02</div><h3>Sophisticated</h3><p>Cool, soulful and polished for elevated receptions and executive events.</p></div>
        <div><div class="number">03</div><h3>Rhythmic</h3><p>More groove, more movement, while still keeping the sound refined.</p></div>
        <div><div class="number">04</div><h3>High Energy</h3><p>Turn it up when the room is ready—with recognizable songs people want to move to.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-top:32px" class="card-grid">
        <div class="card"><div class="number">READ THE ROOM</div><h3>Adapt in real time.</h3><p>We pay attention to the crowd, the pace of the event and the moment—not just a predetermined set list.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><div class="number">BROAD REPERTOIRE</div><h3>Almost any direction.</h3><p>From jazz and soul to pop, rock, reggae, R&B, country, funk, Latin and current hits, the repertoire is intentionally wide.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><div class="number">MAKE IT MEMORABLE</div><h3>Recognizable. Unexpected.</h3><p>Guests know the songs. The Countertone treatment gives them a reason to remember the performance.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section light">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">The musical conversation</div>
        <h2>One melody starts it. Two musicians take it somewhere new.</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">John carries the vocal and guitar foundation. Shawn responds with improvised melodic lines—sometimes echoing, sometimes countering, sometimes leaving space, sometimes pushing the energy forward.</p>
        <p class="bio">It creates the feeling of two musicians listening to each other in the moment rather than simply playing over a backing track. That interaction is the heart of Countertone.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="sound-visual">
        <div class="tag">A visual metaphor for the sound</div>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 700 430" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M-10 280 C 90 150, 170 360, 285 220 S 485 85, 710 235" fill="none" stroke="#e5cd98" stroke-opacity=".82" stroke-width="3"/>
          <path d="M-10 180 C 110 320, 210 80, 330 200 S 520 350, 710 155" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-opacity=".52" stroke-width="2"/>
          <path d="M-10 345 C 110 210, 240 340, 350 280 S 545 150, 710 300" fill="none" stroke="#c8a968" stroke-opacity=".42" stroke-width="2"/>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="repertoire">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Repertoire with range</div>
        <h2>From 1950s classics to today's hits.</h2>
        <p class="section-lead dark-copy">The repertoire is intentionally broad. The common thread isn't a single genre—it is the Countertone approach to familiar songs.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="repertoire">
        <span class="pill">Jazz</span><span class="pill">Soul & R&B</span><span class="pill">Pop</span><span class="pill">Rock</span><span class="pill">Funk & Disco</span><span class="pill">Reggae & Island</span><span class="pill">Country</span><span class="pill">Singer-Songwriter</span><span class="pill">Latin</span><span class="pill">Current Hits</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-list" style="margin-top:38px">
        <div class="song">Time After Time <span>— Cyndi Lauper</span></div>
        <div class="song">Redemption Song <span>— Bob Marley</span></div>
        <div class="song">Black Magic Woman <span>— Santana</span></div>
        <div class="song">Thriller <span>— Michael Jackson</span></div>
        <div class="song">Everybody Wants to Rule the World <span>— Tears for Fears</span></div>
        <div class="song">Levitating <span>— Dua Lipa</span></div>
        <div class="song">Tiny Dancer <span>— Elton John</span></div>
        <div class="song">Sweet Child O' Mine <span>— Guns N' Roses</span></div>
        <div class="song">Watermelon Sugar <span>— Harry Styles</span></div>
        <div class="song">A Sky Full of Stars <span>— Coldplay</span></div>
        <div class="song">Ordinary People <span>— John Legend</span></div>
        <div class="song">Don't Stop Believin' <span>— Journey</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="fineprint">A small sample of a much larger repertoire. Songs and arrangements continue to evolve with the event, audience and setting.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section light">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="eyebrow">Choose the right experience</div>
        <h2>Designed for events where the music matters.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <div class="card"><div class="number">01 • CORPORATE</div><h3>Make the event feel intentional.</h3><p>Executive dinners, receptions, client events, brand gatherings and celebrations where polished music should elevate the room without taking it over.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><div class="number">02 • PRIVATE</div><h3>Give your guests something to talk about.</h3><p>Private homes, milestone celebrations, dinners, cocktail parties and upscale gatherings where you want entertainment that feels personal and memorable.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><div class="number">03 • WEDDINGS</div><h3>Beautiful when it should be. Lively when it matters.</h3><p>Cocktail hour, dinner, reception or a special musical moment—tailored to the atmosphere and flow of the celebration.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="shawn">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">The people behind the music</div>
        <h2>Professional enough for the planner. Personal enough for the party.</h2>
        <p class="dark-copy">Countertone is John Dean on acoustic guitar and vocals with Shawn Bennion on trumpet and flugelhorn.</p>
        <p class="dark-copy">Shawn teaches brass at <strong style="color:#f4f0e7">Bonita High School and Ramona Middle School in La Verne</strong>, and his background as a music educator shapes how he approaches every event: plan ahead, communicate clearly, arrive early, adapt when things change, and make the experience easy for the client.</p>
        <p class="dark-copy">He performs throughout Southern California as a solo artist and with multiple ensembles, including <strong style="color:#f4f0e7">Shawn Bennion & His High Flying Aces</strong>.</p>
        <div class="trust">
          <div class="trustbox"><strong>Prepared</strong><span class="dark-copy">Clear details, advance planning and dependable execution.</span></div>
          <div class="trustbox"><strong>Flexible</strong><span class="dark-copy">Music and energy adjusted to the room and the moment.</span></div>
          <div class="trustbox"><strong>Easy to work with</strong><span class="dark-copy">Straightforward communication from inquiry to final note.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="video-shell" style="background:linear-gradient(145deg,#15181e,#0b0d10)">
          <div class="play">▶</div>
          <small>Place Shawn / Countertone video here</small>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta" id="contact">
    <div class="wrap cta-inner">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Let's create the right atmosphere.</div>
        <h2>Tell me what you're planning.</h2>
        <p class="section-lead dark-copy">Send your date, location and the kind of atmosphere you’re imagining. I’ll get back to you within 24 hours with ideas and availability.</p>
        <p class="dark-copy">For premium events, we can also discuss the best Countertone configuration for the setting, timing and desired energy.</p>
      </div>
      <form>
        <input class="field" type="text" placeholder="Your name" aria-label="Your name" />
        <input class="field" type="email" placeholder="Email" aria-label="Email" />
        <input class="field" type="text" placeholder="Event date" aria-label="Event date" />
        <input class="field" type="text" placeholder="Location / venue" aria-label="Location or venue" />
        <textarea class="field" placeholder="Tell me a little about the event and the atmosphere you want to create." aria-label="Event details"></textarea>
        <button class="btn primary" type="button">Check My Date</button>
        <div class="fineprint">Replace this form with your booking / inquiry form, Calendly, or CRM capture.</div>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <div class="wrap footerin">
      <div>© Countertone • Southern California</div>
      <div>music.shawnbennion.com</div>
    </div>
  </footer>
